    <briefdescription>
<para>Classic separate-chaining hash table used by the engine&apos;s low-level C code paths. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="struct_t_a26e23de58526d847534987d9531aef51_1a26e23de58526d847534987d9531aef51" kindref="member">size</ref></computeroutput> is the bucket count and <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_t_ac165cb2e47175ce65b25465d5bd8556d_1ac165cb2e47175ce65b25465d5bd8556d" kindref="member">length</ref></computeroutput> the live entry count; <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_t_ad0c05772826e7539be987c395607788e_1ad0c05772826e7539be987c395607788e" kindref="member">cmp</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_t_ac312863f3d6a86d9b3b7390129c76334_1ac312863f3d6a86d9b3b7390129c76334" kindref="member">hash</ref></computeroutput> are the key comparison and hashing function pointers; <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_t_a435a16de233b71e17a5186f56adea071_1a435a16de233b71e17a5186f56adea071" kindref="member">timestamp</ref></computeroutput> is bumped on every mutation so iterators can detect concurrent changes. <computeroutput>buckets</computeroutput> is an array of <computeroutput>binding*</computeroutput> heads, each chain holding the <computeroutput>(key, value)</computeroutput> pairs that hash to that slot. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
